{%- comment -%}
  THE check for "is the signed-in Shopify customer an approved B2B customer?" - every wholesale price, carton size,
  B2B cart line, minimum order and pallet promotion is rendered (server-side, by Shopify) only when this says true.
  Outputs "true" or "false". Usage:
    capture np_b2b_check
      render 'np-b2b-customer'
    endcapture
    if np_b2b_check contains 'true'

  - Shopify B2B (customer.b2b?, a company location on Shopify Plus): always trusted.
  - Customer tag (Theme settings > B2B / wholesale > customer tag) - but a tag alone is NOT enough while the B2B
    verification service is configured: Shopify's storefront forms (newsletter / contact) let a visitor add tags to
    their own customer record, so the service also writes b2b.status (approved_auto / approved_manual /
    approved_legacy, set only through the Admin API) and a suspended / rejected / pending company has none of those.
  - Without the service (settings.b2b_endpoint empty) the owner approves by adding the tag by hand, so the tag counts.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign np_b2b = false
  if customer
    if customer.b2b?
      assign np_b2b = true
    elsif customer.tags contains settings.b2b_customer_tag
      assign np_b2b_endpoint = settings.b2b_endpoint | strip
      if np_b2b_endpoint == blank
        assign np_b2b = true
      else
        assign np_b2b_status = customer.metafields.b2b.status.value | append: ''
        if np_b2b_status contains 'approved'
          assign np_b2b = true
        endif
      endif
    endif
  endif
  echo np_b2b
-%}
